# WaterBrain — Read These First

At the start of every new chat about this project, read both files
below. They are the ground truth for project conventions and pending
work. Skip this and you will re-litigate decisions already made.

1. **`.cursor/context-primer.md`** — non-obvious conventions
   (deploy/ship workflow, BF calibration story of v0.3.0 → v0.3.2,
   how the mash pH model actually works, localStorage schema, UI
   conventions, reference recipes for regression testing, where to
   tune what).

2. **`.cursor/todos.md`** — open work items and current status.
   Mirror these into your in-chat todo list. When work completes,
   update this file so the next agent has ground truth.

## Project neighbors (do not confuse)

- **This repo (`WaterBrain/`)** — pure-JS standalone brew-day water
  calculator. Deploys as a static site on GitHub Pages, live at
  <https://keglevelmonitor.github.io/waterbrain/>. Active development.
- **`../FermTrend/`** — sibling standalone web app for BF SG-trend
  and final-gravity analysis. Same visual language, same Pages-based
  deploy pattern. WaterBrain's `ship.ps1`, `local.ps1`, and
  `.github/workflows/pages.yml` were adapted from here — when a
  deploy or scaffolding question comes up, consult FermTrend.
- **`keglevelmonitor/waterbrain` branch `streamlit-legacy` on GitHub**
  — the ORIGINAL Streamlit-based WaterBrain, preserved for
  provenance. Do not build off it; the pure-JS rewrite in `main` is
  the ground truth for behavior. When math differs, this repo wins.
- **`../FermentationVaultPico/`** — Cole's Raspberry Pi Pico W fermentation
  controller. Unrelated to WaterBrain's math, but shares the same
  visual language / dark-theme-with-amber-accent aesthetic. Follow
  the same UX conventions if you touch styling.

## Update discipline

If you make a decision that future agents need to know about (new
convention, gotcha discovered, architectural choice), add it to
`.cursor/context-primer.md`. If you add or resolve a work item,
update `.cursor/todos.md`. These files are the handoff protocol.
